# p_3f8a — Thursday Evening Gathering: Yuki Hosts, Friends at the Table

Marco is at his afternoon-to-night shift (out 13:40–23:00) when the friends arrive, so Yuki hosts alone. The gathering runs roughly 18:00–22:00. The kitchen table seats more than two: extra plates, glasses, and bowls come out of the cupboard, the serving dish joins the table, and the snack bowl and board game leave their resting spots for the coffee table. Yuki is in the kitchen from about 17:00 preparing and serving; the pan, cutting board, spatula, and knife cycle through the counter and sink during the 19:00–21:00 cooking window. The dog stays in the living room or kitchen floor. Marco arrives at 23:00, after the guests have gone or are winding down.

What sets this document apart: it is the only one that predicts the board game at the coffee table, the serving dish at the kitchen table, and the snack bowl at the coffee table during the evening window. A normal weekday has those objects at the bookshelf, cupboard, and cupboard respectively. If the robot sees the board game still on the bookshelf at 19:00–21:00 on Thursday, this document is refuted.

What would refute it: the board game, serving dish, and snack bowl all remain at their resting spots through 18:00–22:00 on Thursday; or Yuki is not in the kitchen at 18:00–20:00.

