# p_5d1b — Kitchen Rhythm: Lunch at Twelve, Dinner at Nineteen

The two residents share the kitchen in two main windows. Morning-to-noon (10:00–12:00) both are present: mugs and bowls are at the table, the dog bowl is at the counter (being filled), the dog food bag is at the pantry, Yuki's tablet is at the table, and the baking tray and mixing bowl appear at the counter around 12:00 (lunch prep or a small bake). After lunch (12:00–14:00) the dog bowl is at the kitchen table (dog eats), the baking tray moves to the table, and the mixing bowl goes to the sink (washing up).

The afternoon (14:00–16:00) is Yuki alone: her glass is at the counter, her plate is at the sink (light snack or prep), the mixing bowl is still at the sink, and the baking tray is at the table. Marco is at work.

Dinner (19:00–21:00) is the second cooking window: the pan moves from the cupboard to the counter, the cutting board goes from the counter to the sink, the spatula comes out of the drawer to the counter, the kitchen knife goes from the drawer to the sink, and plates and glasses are at the table. By 22:00 everything is put away: pan back to pantry or cupboard, cutting board back to counter, spatula back to drawer, knife back to drawer or cupboard.

The dog food bag is on the kitchen floor overnight (00:00–08:00), moves to the pantry by 10:00 (after the morning feeding), and returns to the floor by 20:00 (evening feeding). The dog bowl mirrors this: floor overnight, counter at 10:00 (filling), kitchen table at 12:00 (eating), floor the rest of the day.

What sets this document apart: it is the only one that places the dog bowl at the counter at 10:00 and at the kitchen table at 12:00, and the only one that tracks the pan's three-position cycle (pantry → cupboard → counter → cupboard). If the robot finds the dog bowl on the floor at 10:00 or the pan at the counter at 14:00, this document is refuted.

What would refute it: the dog bowl is at the floor at 10:00–11:00; the pan is at the counter before 19:00; the baking tray is at the counter before 11:00 on a weekday.

